DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260527T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260527T110000
SUMMARY:OpenClawNet - Automation + Azure + Foundry
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nIn this session we will make the ag
 ent production-ready. We will add job scheduling as a background service\,
  integrate Azure OpenAI and Azure AI Foundry as cloud model providers\, bu
 ild monitoring dashboards\, and write unit tests that verify the entire st
 ack.\n\nAt the end we will have a complete\, tested\, cloud-ready agent pl
 atform with production-grade error handling\, multiple AI model providers\
 , scheduled automation\, and observability dashboards. Deploy it to Azure 
 Container Apps\, App Service\, or run it on-premises with Ollama.\n\n**Key
  Topics & Technologies:**\n- BackgroundService for long-running jobs\n- Az
 ure OpenAI integration and model selection\n- Azure AI Foundry (inference\
 , deployments\, evaluation)\n- Unit testing patterns for agents and tools\
 n- Health checks and system diagnostics\n- Job queuing and status tracking
 \n- Configuration for multi-environment deployments (local\, staging\, pro
 duction)\n\nPre-requisites:\n- **Experience:** Intermediate C# and ASP.NET
  Core knowledge (not a .NET 101)\n- **Environment:** .NET 10 SDK\, VS Code
  + GitHub Copilot (or Visual Studio)\, Docker (for Ollama)\n- **Optional:*
 * Azure subscription (for Sessions 3–4\, but local development works fin
 e throughout)\n- **Mindset:** Curiosity about AI agents\, willingness to f
 ollow along live and ask questions
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3139
 46136/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260325T180727Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260325T180727Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Microsoft Reactor Toronto
UID:event_314046561@meetup.com
